> 
How to play
- Black moves first, then the players take turns.
- A man moves one square diagonally forward onto an empty square.
- A piece captures by jumping over an enemy piece next to it and landing
  on the empty square right behind. If that piece can jump again from
  where it landed, it has to.
- A man that reaches the far row becomes a king (shown as B or R).
  Kings move and capture forwards and backwards.
- You win when your opponent has no pieces or no legal move left.
- The dark squares are numbered row by row from the top left; the
  framed board style in the settings shows the numbers.
- During a game type h to see the extra commands.

